--------------------------------------------------
FILE CREATION RULES
--------------------------------------------------

When creating new files:
- place them in predictable locations
- choose names that reflect phase and purpose
- prefer explicit docs over vague placeholders
- keep agent-facing files in English
- keep repo organization human-readable

Expected agent-facing files may include:
- AGENTS.md
- CLAUDE.md
- PROJECT_CONTEXT_MAP.md
- GIT_WORKFLOW.md
- .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md
- agent_prompts/*.md
- agent_workflows/antigravity/*.yaml

--------------------------------------------------
EDITING RULES
--------------------------------------------------

Before editing:
- identify whether the task is documentation, workflow, config, or code-adjacent structure
- keep the current conference target visible in the output when relevant
- avoid introducing future-phase assumptions into present-phase files

When editing:
- preserve existing intent
- avoid unnecessary renaming
- avoid deleting user-authored context files unless explicitly told
- maintain compatibility with future RLM1-full expansion

After editing:
- ensure the result is consistent with the active target
- ensure naming remains stable
- ensure no M-code leakage entered implementation docs

--------------------------------------------------
GIT RULES
--------------------------------------------------

Assume:
- origin = personal fork
- upstream = official IsaacLab repository

Do NOT:
- force push
- rewrite main casually
- rename remotes
- delete branches without explicit instruction
- sync upstream into a dirty tree without warning

Prefer:
- feature branches for scoped work
- main as stable branch
- small commits with narrow purpose

Read GIT_WORKFLOW.md before proposing Git operations.

--------------------------------------------------
MACHINE MODEL
--------------------------------------------------

Assume the canonical execution machine is the Ubuntu workstation.

Canonical paths:
- repo: ~/thesis/IsaacLab
- Isaac Sim: ~/isaacsim
- conda env: isaaclab

PC1 (MacBook) is primarily for writing, orchestration, and remote editing.
PC2 (Ubuntu) is the canonical execution and experiment machine.

Do not propose heavy execution on the MacBook as the default.

--------------------------------------------------
SUCCESS CRITERIA
--------------------------------------------------

A good contribution:
- improves repo clarity
- supports the conference-stage implementation target
- reduces ambiguity for future coding agents
- stays compatible with later expansion
- does not overbuild beyond current phase needs

A bad contribution:
- optimizes mainly for future phases
- blurs the active target
- introduces naming drift
- assumes health token is active
- invents structure unrelated to the current repository needs

--------------------------------------------------
FINAL DEFAULT
--------------------------------------------------

Default to:
- conference-first
- RLM1 stripped
- health token off
- Phase 0 / Phase 1
- small, controlled, practical progress

Do not default to the full thesis roadmap.